u can be in more trouble by being a good cop than a bad cop if the rules are to the detriment of the public.  The &amp;#39;new&amp;#39; police behavior - go for lethal force - might be due to this secret society mentality.  &amp;quot;Good&amp;quot; cops are not valued by questionable influences within the lodges where orders come come from a little old man behind the curtain who appears to be turning the screws on everyone, everywhere... Would someone please arrest that little guy before he destroys the planet?  He needs to be put in &amp;quot;time out&amp;quot;, isolated and have his inner psychopath removed.  </content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3261121678580083400/comments/default/6432311845764178971'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/3261121678580083400/comments/default/6432311845764178971'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2014/08/why-good-cops-stay-silent-persecution.html?showComment=1410152238118#c6432311845764178971' title=''/><author><name>Anonymous</name><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.com/img/blank.gif'/></author><thr:in-reply-to xmlns:thr='http://purl.org/syndication/thread/1.0' href='http://freedominourtime.blogspot.com/2014/08/why-good-cops-stay-silent-persecution.html' ref='tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-3261121678580083400' source='http://www.blogger.com/feeds/32869165/posts/default/3261121678580083400' type='text/html'/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.itemClass" value="pid-530140603"/><gd:extendedProperty name="blogger.displayTime" value="September 7, 2014 at 10:57 PM"/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-32869165.post-8526557739130655515</id><published>2014-09-01T22:38:24.429-06:00</published><updated>2014-09-01T22:38:24.429-06:00</updated><title type='tex